Add encode-prefill-decode (EPD) routing from upstream PR 266, applied as a cherry-pick
of commit 516f1cb90eefe565c9fc894d72c8748eae25085b ("[Feature] Add EPD
routing with JSON metadata") onto vllm-project/router v0.1.16.1.

CONTEXT: PR 266 introduces an EPD router that lets the operator send a request
with metadata describing its endpoint topology. PR 266 was merged on default
branch but the next released tag (v0.1.16.1) was cut BEFORE 516f1cb landed.
The build has to bridge that gap.

The cherry-pick applies cleanly onto v0.1.16.1 with zero textual conflicts,
because v0.1.16.1's src/config/types.rs, src/config/validation.rs,
src/lib.rs, src/main.rs, src/routers/http/{mod.rs,router.rs,epd.rs},
src/server.rs, and Cargo.toml already carry the upstream shape that 516f1cb
adds; the patch only edits them in ways the merge parent had already
prepared for.

CONTRAST WITH OPTIONS: building from the bare commit 516f1cb would require
the Dockerfile to drop --branch (a bare SHA does not resolve a shallow
refspec) and replace it with a fetch-by-SHA. This 0001 cherry-pick keeps
the existing tag-based Dockerfile flow and survives future v0.1.17+ tag bumps
without revisiting the Dockerfile -- it stops being needed the day upstream
cuts a tag containing 516f1cb.

OPERATOR IMPACT: under the v0.1.16.1 + 0001 + 0002 + 0003 + 0004 stack the
EPD request path is live, /v1/chat/completions honours the operator-declared
endpoint metadata, and the rest of the operator's patches (0002 lazy
Mooncake, 0003 read-only observer endpoint, 0004 Kubernetes discovery
readiness-loss deselect) rebase onto the new tree.

AGAINST: vllm-project/router v0.1.16.1 (commit
91b65ee4bdfbe98863a32a2205dced5dbb249ffe). The image build applies
this patch with git apply; a future upstream tag that absorbs 516f1cb
will fail loudly and surface at build time, not in a cluster.

WHEN TO REMOVE: when upstream cuts a tag whose tree contains the merge
commit 516f1cb (or any descendant that carries the EPD routing feature
on top of an already-tagged release). At that point bump
VLLM_ROUTER_VERSION to that tag and delete this patch file. The cherry-pick
was authored against the parent of v0.1.16.1's relevant files, so the
diff is small and a rebase is unlikely to be needed beyond confirming the
merge sits cleanly inside the next tag.
